\name{cellucid_history_get}
\alias{cellucid_history_get}
\title{Read the history}
\usage{
cellucid_history_get(
  viewer,
  all_branches = FALSE,
  branch,
  cursor,
  fields,
  limit = 200,
  since,
  tracker
)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{all_branches}{Every branch, not only the path to the step shown. \code{TRUE} or \code{FALSE}. Default \code{FALSE}, the viewer's own.}
\item{branch}{The path to this branch's tip (by its name or id) instead of the path to the step shown; not with all_branches. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{cursor}{Where the page starts: the next of the last page (its last step's id); the first page when left out. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{fields}{What to add to each step: params (each parameter in words), notes, bookmark. A vector or list of one of \code{"params"}, \code{"notes"}, \code{"bookmark"} (each once). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{limit}{The steps of one page (200 when left out: well under what a tool result carries). A whole number (at least 1). Default \code{200}, the viewer's own.}
\item{since}{Only the steps recorded at or after this time (milliseconds since 1970: a step's "at"), so a second read lists what came since. A number. Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
\item{tracker}{A tracker by its name or its id (history_summary lists them); the tracker in use when left out. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns what it read: a list of \code{branches}, \code{head} (The step shown now), \code{next} (The cursor of the next page; null on the last), \code{steps} (One page: root first; parents before children), \code{total} (Steps on every page (the path to the step shown, or every branch)), \code{tracker}, \code{trackers}. Cells in it are original positions (0-based rows of the dataset's obs).
}
\description{
The steps taken on this dataset, who took each (person, agent, notebook), branches and the step shown.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{history.get} (History). It reads, and changes nothing: it makes no step of the history.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_history_get(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for what it read.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
